If a patient has a previous-opioid-overdose and a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for the patient then the clinician should discuss an increased-overdose-risk with the patient and should weigh an opioid-benefit against a substantial-opioid-risk for the patient and should incorporate a risk-mitigation-strategy into a management-plan for the patient and should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient and should involve a patient-identified-trusted-family-member in a management-plan for the patient and should increase a monitoring-frequency for the patient and should use a shorter-prescription-duration for the patient.
